called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dispatched from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift 6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mode","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0"},{"type":"text","text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nonisolated init"},{"type":"text","text":" does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”","anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var flag = false"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var flag: Bool = false"},{"type":"text","text":". The same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applies to combined declarations: split "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var a, b: Int"},{"type":"text","text":" into separate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declarations."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)","anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data-protection keychain never prompts. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"type":"text","text":"; for unsigned local\/CI builds add a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"team-prefixed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"text":" entitlement. Details in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing","anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gitignored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dev-tooling"},{"type":"text","text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already built without it, run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift package purge-cache"},{"type":"text","text":" so SwiftPM re-reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the manifest. See the repository’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CONTRIBUTING.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"A-Persisted-app-crashes-only-in-Release","text":"A `@Persisted` app crashes only in Release"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the crash is in fetching, make sure you’re on ≥ 1.3.0: generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Predicate"},{"type":"text","text":" over a protocol-required keypath traps under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-O"},{"type":"text","text":", which is why"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the macro generates a per-model "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiduxFetchDescriptor"},{"type":"text","text":". Run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift test -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" in CI to catch this class of issue — Debug builds and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code"